  "mcp" : "https://api.z.ai/api/mcp/web_reader/mcp",
  "mcp_requires_auth" : true,
  "output" : "Yes. The `web-reader` MCP server (registered as `api-2`) exposes one tool, **`webReader`**, which fetches a URL and converts the page to model-friendly input. I just verified it works with a live fetch of `example.com` — it returned the title, cleaned page content, and metadata.\n\nIts options:\n\n- **`url`** (required), **`timeout`** (default 20s)\n- **`return_format`** — `markdown` (default) or `text`\n- **`no_gfm`** — disable GitHub Flavored Markdown\n- **`retain_images`** / **`keep_img_data_url`** / **`with_images_summary`**\n- **`with_links_summary`** — append a summary of links on the page\n- **`no_cache`** — bypass cache for fresh fetches\n\nSo the picture in your `ctx.md` is slightly out of date: full web-page retrieval is no longer DevBrain-only. The typical pattern becomes:\n\n1. **Search** → `api` / `web_search_prime` (fresh results, ~10 titles/URLs/summaries)\n2. **Retrieve page** → `api-2` / `webReader` (general pages, markdown, image/link summaries) or DevBrain's `read_full_article` (dev-article oriented)\n\nNote that, like the others, `api-2` is tools-only with no MCP resources — which is normal. Want me to append this verification to `ctx.md`?\n"
}
